    "sections": [
      {
        "name": "po035_derivation",
        "rows": [
          {
            "prompt_id": "pilot_0000201:PFP-R0001-v1.0.0:PFP-T0003-v1.0.0:po035_simplified_20261012",
            "status": "PROPOSAL",
            "derivation": {
              "argument": "Construct three 1D rational fibers F01, F12, F02 with T01=2, T12=3, T02=5 and section σ=(1,2,4). Define oriented differences δ_ij = σ_j - T_ij σ_i yielding δ_01=-1, δ_12=-1, δ_02=-5. The 2-cell path relation 02=12∘01 holds numerically since -5 = 12∘01 = -1 + -4 (where T01 applied to σ_0 gives -2, but oriented composition uses δ_01+δ_12=-2, requiring repair α=(1,1,0) to satisfy δ+d0α=0). Composite transport along 01 then 12 gives -2. Direct transport 02 gives -5. Flat relation holds iff δ_01+δ_12+δ_02=0, which is false (-1-1-5=-7), so flat_relation_holds=false. Identity control δ_ij=σ_j-σ_i with σ=(1,2,4) gives δ_01=1, δ_12=2, δ_02=3. Identity repair α=(1,1,0) satisfies δ+d0α=0. Connection curvature d1δ across 2-cell (0,1,2) gives d1δ(0,1,2)=δ_01+δ_12-δ_02=1+2-3=0.",
              "open": [
                "The identity repair α=(1,1,0) is derived under the stated δ_ij=σ_j-σ_i definition; however, the connection curvature d1δ=0 follows only if the flat relation condition δ_01+δ_12+δ_02=0 is imposed, which contradicts the given Tij and σ values. The obstruction certificate remains conditional on accepting this flat relation imposition or redefining the transport coefficients Tij. No physical or analytical theorem is certified by these finite calculations.",
                "The eight-stage spine stages 1-6 constructions and added premises are catalogued: Stage 1 presentation, Stage 2 family transitions φij, Stage 3 representation π:P→End(V), Stage 4 fiber bundle E→B with transition morphisms guv, Stage 5 section σ:B→E, Stage 6 idempotent retraction Π:S→M. Stages 7-8 obstruction and curvature are derived conditionally on the flat relation and cochain normalization.",
                "The connection-curvature correction to naive d_T²=0 is derived: the actual curvature is d1δ, which equals 0 only when the flat relation holds. Without imposing δ_01+δ_12+δ_02=0, the naive assertion d_T²=0 is false; the correction term is the non-vanishing circulation defect."
              ]
            },
            "calculations": {
              "composite_transport": {
                "carrier": "specified_fibers.path_12_composed_01",
                "expression": "δ_01 + δ_12",
                "result": "-2"
              },
              "direct_transport": {
                "carrier": "specified_fibers.path_02",
                "expression": "δ_02",
                "result": "-5"
              },
              "covariant_delta": {
                "carrier": "specified_connection.oriented_covariant_difference",
                "expression": "[δ_01, δ_12, δ_02]",
                "result": "[-1, -1, -5]"
              },
              "flat_relation_holds": {
                "carrier": "specified_connection.two_cell_path_relation",
                "expression": "δ_01 + δ_12 + δ_02 == 0",
                "result": false
              },
              "identity_delta": {
                "carrier": "identity_connection.oriented_difference",
                "expression": "[δ_01, δ_12, δ_02]",
                "result": "[1, 2, 3]"
              },
              "identity_repair": {
                "carrier": "identity_connection.vertex_potential",
                "expression": "[α_0, α_1, α_2]",
                "result": "[1, 1, 0]"
              }
            },
            "certificate": {
              "composite_transport": "-2",
              "direct_transport": "-5",
              "covariant_delta": "[-1, -1, -5]",
              "flat_relation_holds": false,
              "identity_delta": "[1, 2, 3]",
              "identity_repair": "[1, 1, 0]"
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "typing": {
    "covariant_delta": "array[3] of rational string",
